From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linalg: skip immintrin.h on riscv64

include/proxsuite/linalg/dense/core.hpp includes the x86-only
<immintrin.h> unless the target is on an architecture denylist
(`__aarch64__`, `__PPC64__`, `__ppc64__`, `_ARCH_PPC64`) that predates
riscv64, so every translation unit pulling in the dense LDLT headers
fails on riscv64 with `fatal error: immintrin.h: No such file or
directory`. Nothing in the header uses a raw x86 intrinsic: all of its
SIMD goes through simde's portable `simde_mm*` wrappers, which is how
the header already builds on aarch64/ppc64. Add `__riscv` to the same
denylist.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the identical denylist is in Simple-Robotics/proxsuite's own core.hpp, so this should go to the original project rather than the cmake-wheel packaging fork, once a riscv64 wheel is public to point at as evidence]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 include/proxsuite/linalg/dense/core.hpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/proxsuite/linalg/dense/core.hpp b/include/proxsuite/linalg/dense/core.hpp
index 5c43d50..5d99e36 100644
--- a/include/proxsuite/linalg/dense/core.hpp
+++ b/include/proxsuite/linalg/dense/core.hpp
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 #include <proxsuite/linalg/veg/memory/dynamic_stack.hpp>

 #if !(defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__PPC64__) || defined(__ppc64__) ||      \
-      defined(_ARCH_PPC64))
+      defined(_ARCH_PPC64) || defined(__riscv))
 #include <immintrin.h>
 #endif

